<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  RUT_FeverWood_MirrorList.xml    RimUtinni Patches · FEVER_WOOD_MECHANICS_1

  Wires the F3 spike class (RM_CompUseEffect_RevealHazards, compiling and
  proven `src/RimMandrake/EnvironmentalHazards/Source/`) into a real,
  reachable ThingDef — the_fever_wood.md §8's "the mirrors... Sporefall
  sells the list", fever_wood_kit_spec.md F3.

  PATTERN BORROWED, NOT INVENTED, same disclosure as
  src/RimUtinni/UtinniPatches/Defs/ThingDefs_Items/Jawa_ClaimRumour.xml (a
  shipped, owner-accepted precedent for exactly this shape: a one-shot
  readable item, ParentName ResourceBase, CompProperties_Usable +
  CompProperties_UseEffectDestroySelf, real classes confirmed against the
  live 1.6 decompile — RimWorld/CompUsable.cs's UseJob calls
  CompUseEffect.DoEffect on every attached use-effect comp, RimWorld/
  CompUseEffect_DestroySelf.cs consumes the item after use). The engine
  correction the spike pass's own header did not need to make explicit but
  this wiring does: CompUseEffect.DoEffect (RimWorld/CompUseEffect.cs)
  internally casts `props` to `CompProperties_UseEffect`, so the comp
  MUST be declared with that CompProperties class (not plain
  CompProperties) or `base.DoEffect` throws an InvalidCastException the
  first time the item is used — RM_CompUseEffect_RevealHazards's own
  DoEffect calls `base.DoEffect(usedBy)` before its own logic, so this is
  load-bearing, not decorative.

  MayRequire is load-bearing (see RUT_FeverWood_MirrorBreak.xml for the
  same rationale) — mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards ships the compClass
  this def names.

  🔴 REAL SUPPLY LANE NOT WIRED, DOCUMENTED, NOT GUESSED: the spec says
  "stocked at Sporefall/Wildsteam traders via trader-kind XML", but
  Sporefall does not yet exist as an authored settlement or TraderKindDef
  — the_fever_wood.md's own Owed section still lists "Sporefall's treetop
  reframe into their faction canon" as a future canon sitting. Guessing a
  TraderKindDef or a settlement to attach this to would be inventing the
  exact shape the standing rule forbids. Ships the same way
  RUT_Jawa_ClaimRumour shipped v1: a real, spawnable, usable item; trade
  stock is a one-line follow-up once Sporefall exists as a trader.
  Tradeability set to None for the same reason (nothing sells it yet).

  ART: validate_patch.py's installed-defs cross-check caught a real defect in the first draft
  of this file — a vanilla texPath (Things/Item/Special/
  SubpersonaCoreTechprof, the GeneSeeker.xml placeholder route) reads as a
  hard ERROR here rather than GeneSeeker's WARN, because this mod's own
  Textures/ root already owns a "things/" namespace, so the validator
  treats a miss inside it as this mod's own missing file rather than an
  unverifiable vanilla bundle path. Fixed by reusing this mod's OWN already-
  shipped loose texture, Textures/Things/Item/Special/JawaClaimRumour.png
  (RUT_Jawa_ClaimRumour's own art, tinted differently here) — a real file
  on disk, confirmed by the same validator. Real, distinct art rides the
  standing art pipeline, not this pass.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="ResourceBase" MayRequire="mandrake.rm.environmentalhazards">
    <defName>RUT_FeverWood_MirrorList</defName>
    <label>mirror list</label>
    <description>A traders' ledger of which black pools have moved lately — ripples, silences, the mirrors that lied about where they were. Reading it marks the agitated pools on your map for a while. The list is a snapshot; the water keeps its own schedule.</description>
    <thingClass>ThingWithComps</thingClass>
    <graphicData>
      <texPath>Things/Item/Special/JawaClaimRumour</texPath>
      <graphicClass>Graphic_Single</graphicClass>
      <color>(90, 130, 150)</color>
    </graphicData>
    <category>Item</category>
    <thingCategories>
      <li>ItemsMisc</li>
    </thingCategories>
    <tradeability>None</tradeability>
    <selectable>true</selectable>
    <stackLimit>1</stackLimit>
    <statBases>
      <Mass>0.2</Mass>
      <Flammability>1.0</Flammability>
      <MaxHitPoints>40</MaxHitPoints>
      <MarketValue>180</MarketValue>
    </statBases>
    <comps>
      <li Class="CompProperties_Usable">
        <useJob>UseItem</useJob>
        <useLabel>Read the mirror list</useLabel>
      </li>
      <li Class="CompProperties_UseEffectDestroySelf" />
      <li Class="CompProperties_UseEffect">
        <compClass>RimMandrake.EnvironmentalHazards.RM_CompUseEffect_RevealHazards</compClass>
      </li>
    </comps>
  </ThingDef>

</Defs>
